From 542204c3990d8e1551786cbd3f0f4cb8798eec52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 05:08:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Sin City ink: a switchable two-tone art style for 3D
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Learned while building labyrinth-larry's alternate art mode:
- docs/06 §7 Sin City ink house style (roles, hatching, one accent, chrome)
- docs/07 role patch via onBeforeCompile + the ink post-pass recipe
- docs/14 pitfalls 69-74 (linear RT thresholds, accent flood, hero contrast,
  noisy hatching, inherited letter-spacing tween, autopilot vs lava)
- docs/11 surface tiles (tar, grease, wind, coins) with numbers
- docs/12 seven-sin level meta table + new glyphs; docs/05 vanilla settings cog
- kits: ink-two-tone-3d.labyrinth-larry.js, settings-url-override.labyrinth-larry.js
- screenshots under assets/screenshots/labyrinth-larry/

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H4dzeFG8ySTyruxJ1149ob
